    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "The guests are waiting for the chef. Dmitry finds Max hiding and demands a masterpiece. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Витя, просыпайтесь!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Он не проснется.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Бесполезно его будить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Максимилиан, вот вы где.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, я здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Вы прячетесь от нас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я ни от кого не прячусь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Приготовьте нам маленький шедевр.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Мы хотим старинную французскую кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф-повару нужно отдыхать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "У нас производственное совещание.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Максимилиан, я вас жду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас к вам приду.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Витя, просыпайтесь!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vitya, wake up!' The character uses the imperative command form of the verb meaning 'wake up'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Он не проснется.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He will not wake up.' Dmitry combines 'he' with 'wake up' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Бесполезно его будить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is useless to wake him.' Dmitry links 'useless' directly with 'him' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Максимилиан, вот вы где.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maximilian, there you are.' The question opens with the interrogative word for 'where' and builds toward 'where'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, я здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I am here.' Notice how 'yes' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'here'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Вы прячетесь от нас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are hiding from us.' Dmitry uses the imperative command form of the verb meaning 'to hide'. Then Max responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я ни от кого не прячусь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am not hiding from anyone.' The negative particle sits directly before the verb for 'to hide' to negate the action.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Приготовьте нам маленький шедевр.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Prepare a little masterpiece for us.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'prepare' with 'masterpiece'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Мы хотим старинную французскую кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We want classic French cuisine.' Notice how 'we' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'kitchen'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф-повару нужно отдыхать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A chef needs to rest.' Max combines 'head chef' with 'relax' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Then Dmitry responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "У нас производственное совещание.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have a production meeting.' Dmitry links 'at' directly with 'us' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vova",
      "t": "Максимилиан, я вас жду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maximilian, I am waiting for you.' Dmitry uses the polite plural 'you' here alongside 'person name', keeping a formal or respectful tone.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас к вам приду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will come to you now.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'I' with 'will come'. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
